    "title": "\"Life-changing,\" Monett Fire gets new extrication equipment - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Mike Olmstead No media credit provided. ,\n9 hours ago\nMONETT, Mo. — New equipment is put to the test by the Monett Fire Department.\nIt was able to recently purchase a full set of battery-powered extrication tools, which includes a “combi,” that’s a combination cutter and spreader, and a ram extension kit.\nThe in-service training Wednesday entailed Monett and Purdy firefighters working with some of the equipment so they could get better familiar it. Training also took place on Monday and will happen again next week.\nSo, just how important are the new additions?\n“This equipment is life-changing. And, I mean that as important as possible to our citizens and visitors. We were using hydraulic. If you have a wreck down an embankment, or anything like that, you have to carry the pump. You have to carry the tools and the hoses, and it is manpower draining. With this equipment, we will be able to grab the tools and get to the patients, get to the victims much quicker,” said Capt. Clell Maples, Monett FD.\nExtra batteries also came with each device. The department will keep its set of hydraulic-powered equipment as a backup.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KSNF/KODE | FourStatesHomepage.com.\n3",
